# URL Shortener

Shortens a long URL, stores it in DynamoDB, and redirects visitors to the original address.

## Requirements

- Node.js 18 or newer
- An AWS account
- A DynamoDB table in the same region as `AWS_REGION`

Create the table with partition key `code` (String). The default table name is `urls`.

## Setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/salman14890/url-shortener-nodejs.git
cd url-shortener
npm install
cp .env-example .env

Edit .env and set your own values:

AWS_REGION=eu-west-1
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-aws-access-key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-aws-secret-key
PORT=3000
DYNAMODB_TABLE=urls

RUN

npm run dev

Open http://localhost:3000.

npm start runs the app once. npm run dev restarts it when you change a file.

API
POST /short-url with JSON { "url": "https://example.com" } returns a short code.

GET /:code redirects to the original URL and increments the click count.

GET /stats/:code returns the stored item.